selector_to_html = {"a[href=\"#submodules\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Submodules<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#submodules\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>", "a[href=\"aerothermodynamics/index.html\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">pyskyfire.thermo.aerothermodynamics<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-pyskyfire.thermo.aerothermodynamics\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>CEA-backed gas properties along a rocket-engine contour.</p><p>All public values use base SI units. The old constructor and getter API is\nretained, but the implementation has only one design path and one state path.</p>", "a[href=\"nozzle_loss/index.html\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">pyskyfire.thermo.nozzle_loss<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-pyskyfire.thermo.nozzle_loss\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>Efficiency corrections from ideal (ODE) to delivered engine performance.</p><p>CEA, and therefore <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"aerothermodynamics/Aerothermodynamics.html#pyskyfire.thermo.aerothermodynamics.Aerothermodynamics\" title=\"pyskyfire.thermo.aerothermodynamics.Aerothermodynamics\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Aerothermodynamics</span></code></a>,\nsolves a one-dimensional equilibrium expansion. Real nozzle flow loses\nperformance to two-dimensional divergence, the wall boundary layer and\nfinite-rate chemistry, and real injectors do not release the full ideal\ncombustion energy. The standard engineering treatment is to keep the ideal\nsolution and multiply it by efficiencies obtained from higher-fidelity codes:</p>", "a[href=\"#module-pyskyfire.thermo\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">pyskyfire.thermo<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-pyskyfire.thermo\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>Fluid properties, thermodynamic states and combustion-gas aerothermodynamics.</p><p>CEA-backed APIs are loaded on first access so fluid and nozzle-loss utilities\ncan be imported without loading CEA, including through the package root.</p>", "a[href=\"transport/index.html\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">pyskyfire.thermo.transport<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-pyskyfire.thermo.transport\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><h2>Classes<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#classes\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>", "a[href=\"duty/index.html\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">pyskyfire.thermo.duty<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-pyskyfire.thermo.duty\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>What a turbomachine is asked to do, before anything is decided about how.</p><p>A duty is the fluid\u2019s side of the contract: the mass flow, the state it\narrives in, the pressure it must leave at and the shaft speed. Everything a\ndesign sizes itself on follows from those four, and <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"duty/MachineDuty.html#pyskyfire.thermo.duty.MachineDuty\" title=\"pyskyfire.thermo.duty.MachineDuty\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">MachineDuty</span></code></a> holds\nthe results in the form designs read:</p>", "a[href=\"state/index.html\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">pyskyfire.thermo.state<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-pyskyfire.thermo.state\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>CoolProp-backed fluid state resolution, including the saturation dome.</p><p>Specific enthalpy and pressure identify states through the boiling dome,\nwhere temperature and pressure alone cannot determine vapour quality.\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">FluidStateResolver</span></code> caches saturation data and resolves bulk states using\nhomogeneous (no-slip) two-phase density. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">probe_fluid</span></code> reports whether the\nbackend supports enthalpy-based resolution and saturation properties.</p>", "a[href=\"eos/index.html\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">pyskyfire.thermo.eos<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-pyskyfire.thermo.eos\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>Equations of state: the thermodynamic relations a design reads a fluid through.</p><p>A turbomachine design needs more of a fluid than its density at one point. It\nneeds the states at either end of the machine, and the state an isentropic\nprocess reaches at the other end, since that fixes the head. A turbine\u2019s\nmeanline also needs the states between its rows, which it knows by enthalpy\nand by the entropy the losses so far have added, and the speed of sound at\neach. An <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"eos/EquationOfState.html#pyskyfire.thermo.eos.EquationOfState\" title=\"pyskyfire.thermo.eos.EquationOfState\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">EquationOfState</span></code></a> answers those questions and returns the\npackage\u2019s <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"state/FluidState.html#pyskyfire.thermo.state.FluidState\" title=\"pyskyfire.thermo.state.FluidState\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">FluidState</span></code></a> each time, so the code\nasking does not care whether the answer came from CoolProp or from a constant.</p>", "a[href=\"fluid/index.html\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">pyskyfire.thermo.fluid<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-pyskyfire.thermo.fluid\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><h2>Classes<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#classes\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>"}
skip_classes = ["headerlink", "sd-stretched-link"]

window.onload = function () {
    for (const [select, tip_html] of Object.entries(selector_to_html)) {
        const links = document.querySelectorAll(` ${select}`);
        for (const link of links) {
            if (skip_classes.some(c => link.classList.contains(c))) {
                continue;
            }

            tippy(link, {
                content: tip_html,
                allowHTML: true,
                arrow: true,
                placement: 'auto-start', maxWidth: 600, interactive: false,
                onShow(instance) {MathJax.typesetPromise([instance.popper]).then(() => {});},
            });
        };
    };
    console.log("tippy tips loaded!");
};
